{"success": true, "data": {"stdout": "{"doc_id": "Granskär", "input_text": "Granskär ( , ) is an island in the Kvarken ( \" The Throat \" ) , the narrowest part of the Gulf of Bothnia in the northern part of the Baltic sea . It has few inhabitants , almost all Swedish - speaking . Granskär belongs to the municipality of Vaasa . The area has been inhabited since before the time of Swedish dominion over Finland ; the first habitations can be traced to at least the 11th century and possibly earlier . Granskär is part of a larger archipelago and most of the smaller islands around Replot have traditionally been used as fishing camps . Today the buildings are generally used as summer cottages since maritime activities play a large part in the culture of the region . Fishing is nowadays mostly a recreational activity , but there are still a number of professional fishermen active in the archipelago . A large part of the Kvarken archipelago has been designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site .", "gold_entities": [{"text": "Granskär", "type": "LOC"}, {"text": "Kvarken", "type": "LOC"}, {"text": "The Throat", "type": "LOC"}, {"text": "Gulf of Bothnia", "type": "LOC"}, {"text": "Baltic", "type": "LOC"}, {"text": "Swedish", "type": "MISC"}, {"text": "Vaasa", "type": "LOC"}, {"text": "Swedish", "type": "LOC"}, {"text": "Finland", "type": "LOC"}, {"text": "11th century", "type": "TIME"}, {"text": "Replot", "type": "LOC"}, {"text": "UNESCO World Heritage Site", "type": "MISC"}], "gold_relations": [{"head": "Gulf of Bothnia", "tail": "Baltic", "type": "P361", "head_type": "LOC", "tail_type": "LOC"}, {"head": "Gulf of Bothnia", "tail": "Kvarken", "type": "P527", "head_type": "LOC", "tail_type": "LOC"}, {"head": "Baltic", "tail": "Gulf of Bothnia", "type": "P527", "head_type": "LOC", "tail_type": "LOC"}, {"head": "Baltic", "tail": "Finland", "type": "P205", "head_type": "LOC", "tail_type": "LOC"}, {"head": "Vaasa", "tail": "Gulf of Bothnia", "type": "P206", "head_type": "LOC", "tail_typ